WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.955
"There are two political groups in Lilliput," began Reldresal, "the High-Heels and the Low-Heels.

2
00:00:06.956 --> 00:00:11.492
The groups are named after the style of shoes their members wear.

3
00:00:11.493 --> 00:00:16.572
"Once, the High-Heels were the most popular group," Reldresal went on.

4
00:00:16.573 --> 00:00:20.703
"Our king and his officials, however, are Low-Heels."

5
00:00:20.704 --> 00:00:23.875
"Do the two groups get along?" I asked.

6
00:00:23.876 --> 00:00:28.295
"Oh no! The two groups hate each other," said Reldresal.

7
00:00:28.296 --> 00:00:33.187
"The king is afraid that the High-Heels may try to take his power."

8
00:00:33.188 --> 00:00:34.613
"And could they?"

9
00:00:34.614 --> 00:00:41.967
"Perhaps. We think that there are more High-Heels than Low-Heels in Lilliput," said Reldresal.

10
00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:47.331
"What’s worse, the king is very upset with his son, the prince of Lilliput.

11
00:00:47.332 --> 00:00:50.407
The prince wears one shoe with a high heel.

12
00:00:50.408 --> 00:00:52.965
His other shoe has a low heel.

13
00:00:52.966 --> 00:00:56.921
That’s why the prince moves up and down as he walks.

14
00:00:56.922 --> 00:01:02.243
"The king also has enemies in other places," Reldresal continued.

15
00:01:02.244 --> 00:01:08.082
"Lilliput and a nearby island, Blefuscu, have been at war for three years."

16
00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:10.146
"That island to the east?"

17
00:01:10.147 --> 00:01:11.984
Reldresal nodded.

18
00:01:11.985 --> 00:01:14.887
"How did this war start?" I asked.

19
00:01:14.888 --> 00:01:20.799
"The war began over how people cut open boiled eggs," Reldresal explained.

20
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.659
"I beg your pardon?"

21
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.866
I thought that I had misunderstood his words.

22
00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:28.176
I was still learning Lilliputian.

23
00:01:28.177 --> 00:01:30.758
"Boiled eggs," he repeated.

24
00:01:30.759 --> 00:01:33.731
"People in Lilliput like to eat boiled eggs.

25
00:01:33.732 --> 00:01:37.616
An egg has a big end and a small, pointed end.

26
00:01:37.617 --> 00:01:42.690
Almost everyone in Lilliput used to cut open their boiled eggs at the big end.

27
00:01:42.691 --> 00:01:47.197
The problem started when our king’s grandfather was a little boy.

28
00:01:47.198 --> 00:01:51.375
He was then the prince of Lilliput, and his father was the king.

29
00:01:51.376 --> 00:01:55.227
One day, the prince cut open his egg at the big end.

30
00:01:55.228 --> 00:01:58.423
He got careless and cut his finger.

31
00:01:58.424 --> 00:02:02.160
The king got very angry because the prince was hurt.

32
00:02:02.161 --> 00:02:05.135
That day, the king made a new law.

33
00:02:05.136 --> 00:02:10.937
From then on, everyone in Lilliput had to cut open their boiled eggs at the small end.

34
00:02:10.938 --> 00:02:14.034
Small-Enders are people who obey the law.

35
00:02:14.035 --> 00:02:17.740
Big-Enders refuse to obey the law."

36
00:02:17.741 --> 00:02:23.694
"I suppose," I said, "that these two groups also hate each other?"

37
00:02:23.695 --> 00:02:28.956
"Correct. Over the years, they have had many fights," said Reldresal.

38
00:02:28.957 --> 00:02:31.589
"Our current king is a Small-Ender.

39
00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:35.549
Some Big-Enders have gone to live in Blefuscu.

40
00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:41.047
The king of Blefuscu would like to take over Lilliput, and the Big-Enders support him.

41
00:02:41.048 --> 00:02:46.854
We have heard rumors that the Blefuscan king plans to attack Lilliput with many ships.

42
00:02:46.855 --> 00:02:49.257
Can you find a way to help us?"

43
00:02:49.258 --> 00:02:53.754
"Reldresal," I said, "I’m sure I can."

44
00:02:53.755 --> 00:02:58.853
He told me that more than fifty ships were in the harbor at Blefuscu.

45
00:02:58.854 --> 00:03:02.784
Only about a kilometer of sea separates the two islands.

46
00:03:02.785 --> 00:03:06.217
The water between them is quite shallow.

47
00:03:06.218 --> 00:03:12.935
For the next few days, I kept away from the shore of Lilliput that is opposite Blefescu.

48
00:03:12.936 --> 00:03:16.153
I did not want the Blefuscans to see me.

49
00:03:16.154 --> 00:03:20.112
I had figured out a plan for helping the king of Lilliput.

50
00:03:20.113 --> 00:03:25.066
But if the Blefuscans knew about me, my plan would fail.

51
00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:28.448
A few days later, I spoke to the king.

52
00:03:28.449 --> 00:03:33.911
"I have a secret plan," I said, "to steal many of the Blefuscan ships.

53
00:03:33.912 --> 00:03:37.738
Then your enemies will not be able to invade Lilliput."

54
00:03:37.739 --> 00:03:42.854
"I would appreciate your help, Enormous One," replied the king.

55
00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:46.639
After I explained my plan, he said,

56
00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:50.460
"Tell me what you need to make your plan work."

57
00:03:50.461 --> 00:03:55.182
"Have your workmen make fifty very large metal hooks," I told him.

58
00:03:55.183 --> 00:03:58.003
"I need lots of strong rope as well."

59
00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:02.817
"Those things will be ready in two days," promised the king.

60
00:04:02.818 --> 00:04:10.303
The look on his face was very serious.

